# Stradivarius violin — buyable / purchasable leads (web research snapshot)

Compiled: 2026-05-14 (automated web search; not an exhaustive crawl of the entire internet).
Genuine Antonio Stradivari violins almost never appear as simple “add to cart” retail. They trade by auction, private treaty through specialist dealers, or confidential private sale. Verify every listing, price, and availability before paying; expect due diligence, deposits, and expert authentication.

---

## 1. Authentic Stradivari violins — documented public sale channels / lots

### Kodner Galleries — “The McKay” (Cremona, c. 1737)

- Catalog lot (Antonio Stradivari violin, “The McKay”, label 1737; estimate on page USD 2,000,000–9,000,000; online bidding not available for this lot — register with gallery, deposit required): https://www.kodner.com/auctions/2025/10/08/stradivarius-violin-estate-jewelry-decoration/81
- Auction context: catalogued under “Stradivarius Violin, Estate Jewelry & Decoration”, 2025-10-08, Dania Beach, Florida. **Confirm whether the sale has concluded and whether the instrument remains available** (e.g. unsold lot, post-sale negotiation).

### Sotheby’s — “Joachim–Ma” (1714)

- Auction / sale hub (Masters Week 2025): https://www.sothebys.com/en/buy/auction/2025/the-joachim-ma-stradivarius-a-masterpiece-of-sound
- Lot page (same sale): https://www.sothebys.com/buy/ce9ed3bd-5031-43ec-bf46-a0af012b949b/lots/e2c3308d-a2a2-4625-98d6-aecba2711ae2
- Press coverage indicates this violin **sold at auction in February 2025** (order-of-magnitude price reported around USD 11.25–11.3 million including premium). **Not a current retail listing**; retained here as a recent comparable and proof of buyability via major auction.

